    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0275" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/11–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-14T10:00:00+02:00">November 14,
                            1946—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:51 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1569. See mytel 1499, November 2.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d182-f1"/> PriMin in talk
                    with me last evening brought up question of his visiting US and I read him
                    essential parts of Deptel 1403 of October 30. He replied that after seeing how
                    events develop here in near future and before making final decision he will
                    again talk with me. However, he feels at present that since solution of Greece’s
                    main problems both as regards security and reconstruction depend principally on
                    decisions to be made in New York<anchor n="42" xml:id="d182-f2"/> and Washington
                    he would risk important loss of prestige here <pb facs="0276" n="264"
                        xml:id="pg264"/> where politics are so largely personal if he failed to go
                    to US at least for brief period at this critical juncture.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
